\title{Provide On-Demand Result Frames for an \code{IdfViewer}}
\description{
\code{IdfViewerFrameProvider} keeps result queries and their DuckDB connections
independent from an HTTP framework. Use \verb{$metadata()} to build the browser
payload, \verb{$fetch()} in an HTTP adapter to obtain one or more aggregated
Float32 frames, and \verb{$close()} when the application no longer serves the
viewer.
}
\details{
Frame and variable indices are zero-based so an HTTP adapter can pass browser query
parameters directly to \verb{$fetch()}. Invalid requests raise an
\code{eplusr_error_viewer_frame} condition with an integer \code{status} field suitable
for the HTTP response status.
}
